<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills sold out, yield falls.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills sold out, yield falls.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry issue of three-month discount T-bills was sold out at Monday's auction, yielding 1.53 percent to maturity, finance ministry figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yields to maturity of the respective issue auctioned on July 7 was 1.75 percent.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par value of 40 billion levs and was heavily oversubscribed.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p>Issue number BG3041197008</p>
<p> Maturity			three months</p>
<p> Par value		     40,000 million levs</p>
<p> Auction date		  July 14</p>
<p> Issue date		    July 16</p>
<p> Maturity date		 October 15</p>
<p> Bids received		 90,130 million levs</p>
<p> Average price of bids     98.36 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 40,000 million levs</p>
<p> Average accepted price    98.49 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity  1.53 pct</p>
<p>NOTE:</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
